                "summary": "- Joan Carroll was an American child actress born on January 18, 1931, in Elizabeth, New Jersey.\n- She began her film career in 1936 and was active until retiring in 1950.\n- She appeared in classic films such as *Meet Me in St. Louis* (1944) and *The Bells of St. Mary's* (1945).\n- She also starred in *Primrose Path* (1940) and *Obliging Young Lady* (1941), and was the first child star to lead a Broadway musical, *Panama Hattie* (1940–1942).\n- She was known for her singing and tap-dancing skills, trained at the Fanchon and Marco Dancing School in Hollywood.\n- Joan Carroll died on November 16, 2016, in Puerto Vallarta, Mexico, at the age of 85.",
